[00:10.73]I Heard the Bells on Christmas Day
[00:16.00]Their old familiar carols play,
[00:21.52]And wild and sweet the words repeat
[00:27.23]Of peace on earth, good will to men.
[00:38.84]I thought how, as the day had come,
[00:43.74]The belfries of all Christendom
[00:49.51]Had rolled along the unbroken song
[00:55.46]Of peace on earth, good will to men.
[01:06.68]And in despair I bowed my head:
[01:13.16]There is no peace on earth, I said,
[01:21.09]For hate is strong and mocks the song
[01:27.67]Of peace on earth, good will to men.
[01:45.65]Then pealed the bells more loud and deep:
[01:50.68]God is not dead, nor does he sleep
[01:56.04]The wrong shall fail, the right prevail,
[02:03.12]With peace on earth, good will to men
[02:24.02]
